UID:mondriaan-publication-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135731Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260730
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260731
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: Publication
DESCRIPTION:The Mondriaan Fund's Publication grant supports the production 
 of special publications about living visual artists from the Netherlands o
 r the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. It funds books and other publications
  that give substantial\, high-quality attention to an artist's work and pr
 actice. WHO CAN APPLY: visual artists and publishers\, individually or joi
 ntly\; the featured artist(s) must be professional and have been active fo
 r at least one year\, based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of th
 e Kingdom. AMOUNT: the Mondriaan Fund contributes a maximum of 35% of the 
 eligible expenses\; the available budget for this round is EUR 205\,000. A
 PPLYING: submitted through the Mondriaan Fund's online application portal\
 , which requires a pre-created account (allow several working days to set 
 up). DEADLINE: 30 July 2026\, 16:00 Dutch time (10:00 Caribbean time).\n\n
 Organisation: Mondriaan Fund (Mondriaan Fonds)\nLocation: Netherlands. Fea
 tured artist(s) must be professional visual artists based in the Netherlan
 ds or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom\; publishers may co-apply.\nAward:
  Contribution of up to 35% of eligible expenses. Total budget for this rou
 nd is EUR 205\,000.\nDuration: Project-based (production of a publication)
 .\n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/publi
 cation-2/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/publication-2
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands. Featured artist(s) must be professional visual artist
 s based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom\; publishe
 rs may co-apply.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-residency-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135731Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260827
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: Residency
DESCRIPTION:The Mondriaan Fund's Residency grant supports professional visu
 al artists\, curators\, and art observers who want to deepen their practic
 e through a residency in the Netherlands or abroad. It contributes to the 
 costs of a self-arranged residency that offers meaningful development for 
 the applicant's work. WHO CAN APPLY: visual artists\, curators\, and art o
 bservers who have been professionally active for at least one year and are
  based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. AMOUNT: th
 e grant amount varies depending on the residency's location and duration\;
  applicants must contribute at least 10% of the costs themselves\, through
  personal investment\, third-party contributions\, an interest-free loan\,
  or crowdfunding. APPLYING: submitted through the Mondriaan Fund's online 
 application portal\, which requires a pre-created account (allow several w
 orking days). DEADLINE: 27 August 2026\, 16:00 Dutch time (11:00 Caribbean
  time).\n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan Fund (Mondriaan Fonds)\nLocation: Nethe
 rlands. Applicants must be based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part 
 of the Kingdom\; residencies may take place in the Netherlands or abroad.\
 nAward: Grant amount varies depending on the location and duration of the 
 residency. Applicants must contribute at least 10% themselves (personal in
 vestment\, third-party contributions\, an interest-free loan\, or crowdfun
 ding).\nDuration: Varies by residency.\n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds
 .nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/residency/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/residency/?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands. Applicants must be based in the Netherlands or the Ca
 ribbean part of the Kingdom\; residencies may take place in the Netherland
 s or abroad.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rijkscultuurfondsen-interdisciplinary-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135731Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Deadline: Rijkscultuurfondsen: Interdisciplinary Grant
DESCRIPTION:The Interdisciplinary grant is a new joint scheme of the six Du
 tch national cultural funds (Mondriaan Fund\, Performing Arts Fund NL\, Fu
 nd for Cultural Participation\, Netherlands Film Fund\, Creative Industrie
 s Fund NL\, and the Dutch Foundation for Literature)\, announced on 7 July
  2026. It supports makers and organisations whose work genuinely crosses t
 he boundaries of the individual funds' disciplines (visual art\, design\, 
 film\, literature\, performing arts\, and cultural participation) and cann
 ot be contained within a single discipline. TWO TRACKS: an Individual trac
 k for professional makers with a demonstrable interdisciplinary practice (
 at least one year of experience\; income cap EUR 55\,000 including the gra
 nt\; approximately EUR 24\,900 for 12 months)\; and an Organisation track 
 for organisations running multi-discipline projects. AMOUNT: EUR 12\,500 t
 o 50\,000 per project. ELIGIBILITY: makers and organisations based in the 
 Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. APPLYING: handled throug
 h the Mondriaan Fund's online application portal (info@mondriaanfonds.nl)\
 ; an account is required in advance. DEADLINE: 1 October 2026\, 16:00 Dutc
 h time (single application round).\n\nOrganisation: Dutch national cultura
 l funds (Rijkscultuurfondsen)\, via the Mondriaan Fund\nLocation: Netherla
 nds. For professional makers and organisations based in the Netherlands or
  the Caribbean part of the Kingdom whose practice spans multiple disciplin
 es.\nAward: EUR 12\,500 to 50\,000 per project. The individual-maker track
  is approximately EUR 24\,900 for 12 months (income cap EUR 55\,000 includ
 ing the grant).\nDuration: Up to 12 months for the individual-maker track.
 \n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/interd
 isciplinary/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/interdiscipli
 nary/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands. For professional makers and organisations based in th
 e Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom whose practice spans mu
 ltiple disciplines.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:arts-council-ireland-visual-arts-project-award-2027@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135731Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260723
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260724
SUMMARY:Deadline: Arts Council of Ireland: Visual Arts Project Award 2027
DESCRIPTION:The Arts Council of Ireland's Visual Arts Project Award funds p
 rofessional visual artists\, curators\, and producers to develop and deliv
 er visual arts projects\, in three strands: planning and pre-production (u
 p to EUR 12\,000)\, production and engagement (up to EUR 60\,000)\, and pa
 rtnership production (up to EUR 150\,000). Primarily aimed at applicants b
 ased in the Republic of Ireland\, but the Arts Council's standard eligibil
 ity clause allows applicants based elsewhere where the application explici
 tly demonstrates how the outcomes will benefit the arts in Ireland. The wi
 der Project Award 2027 covers nine disciplines including film and music on
  a similar timeline. Deadline 23 July 2026\, 17:30 Irish time.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: Arts Council of Ireland / An Chomhairle Ealaion\nLocation: Republic 
 of Ireland. Applicants based outside Ireland may apply if the application 
 clearly shows how outcomes benefit the arts in the Republic of Ireland.\nA
 ward: Three strands: up to EUR 12\,000 (planning and pre-production)\, up 
 to EUR 60\,000 (production and engagement)\, up to EUR 150\,000 (partnersh
 ip production). No application fee.\nDuration: Projects delivered in 2027.
 \n\nMore: https://artscouncil.ie/funding-opportunities/project-award/visua
 l-arts-project-award/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=ref
 erral
URL:https://artscouncil.ie/funding-opportunities/project-award/visual-arts-
 project-award/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Republic of Ireland. Applicants based outside Ireland may apply if
  the application clearly shows how outcomes benefit the arts in the Republ
 ic of Ireland.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ctm-2027-radio-lab-in-listening@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135731Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260906
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260907
SUMMARY:Deadline: In Listening 2027: Call for Hybrid Radio/Live Works (CTM 
 Festival\, Berlin)
DESCRIPTION:In Listening is the renamed successor to the CTM Radio Lab\, af
 ter more than a decade of collaboration between CTM Festival and Germany's
  public radio Deutschlandfunk Kultur\, with support from Austria's ORF\, z
 eroing in on sound-focused experiences. This open call is for works strong
 ly grounded in experimental sound practices and audio art and driven by co
 nceptual approaches or sonic narratives\, exploring the blurred edges betw
 een sound\, noise\, music\, storytelling\, poetry\, and documenting\, wher
 e sound is the main medium. Works should respond to the CTM 2027 theme 'Pr
 ocess...ing'\, with active listening informing the proposals. Applications
  should describe how the work could be developed for two complementary out
 puts: a LIVE EVENT at CTM 2027 and a RADIO BROADCAST on Deutschlandfunk Ku
 ltur and Oe1/ORF. At CTM\, works are presented in the silent green Kuppelh
 alle with an intimate setup\, the audience seated around the performer(s) 
 and surrounded by a 6.1-channel PA (creative use of fewer channels\, stere
 o\, or mono is welcome\; minimal lighting and scenography or performances 
 in the dark are suitable\, but video and complex scenography are out of sc
 ope). For radio/podcast\, proposals should consider the individual listeni
 ng experience (a recording of the performance is not sufficient)\; the bro
 adcast is a 40-55 minute piece aired in a late-night slot to a largely Ger
 man-speaking\, non-specialist audience. Works premiere at CTM 2027 (22-31 
 January 2027\, Berlin)\, are broadcast in Deutschlandfunk Kultur's Klangku
 nst programme in Spring 2027\, and presented via ORF (Oe1 Zeit-Ton or Blau
 e Stunde / Kunstradio) and/or ORF musikprotokoll im steirischen herbst in 
 Graz (Autumn 2027)\, then available for streaming for at least one year. B
 UDGET: two selected works each receive EUR 6\,000\; winners give up to two
  performances at CTM. Group proposals are possible but should keep a modes
 t travel budget. JURY: Jan Rohlf (CTM)\, Marcus Gammel (Deutschlandfunk Ku
 ltur)\, Anna Soucek (ORF Oe1)\, and one independent artist. TIMELINE: dead
 line 6 September 2026 at 23:59 Berlin time\; winners announced mid-October
  2026\; remote production late October 2026 to January 2027. APPLY (in Eng
 lish\, PDF\, max 20MB) with a project description including rough budget (
 max 4 pages)\, technical requirements\, and CV\; questions to in_listening
 @ctm-festival.de. No application fee.\n\nOrganisation: CTM Festival with D
 eutschlandfunk Kultur and ORF\nLocation: Berlin\, Germany. Premiered at CT
 M 2027 and broadcast on Deutschlandfunk Kultur\, with onward presentation 
 via ORF Oe1 (Zeit-Ton or Blaue Stunde / Kunstradio) and/or ORF musikprotok
 oll im steirischen herbst in Graz. Applications accepted internationally\,
  submitted in English.\nAward: Two selected works are each supported by a 
 fee of EUR 6\,000. CTM covers travel to Berlin and lodging during the prod
 uction and festival periods\; technical and staging costs for the CTM pres
 entation (and possible ORF musikprotokoll presentation) are covered separa
 tely by arrangement. Research\, creation and collaborator costs are the ar
 tist's own. Radio-production support (translations\, voiceovers\, studio t
 ime) can be provided by Deutschlandfunk Kultur upon discussion. No applica
 tion fee.\nDuration: Work premiered at CTM Festival 22-31 January 2027\; r
 adio broadcast Spring 2027\; ORF/musikprotokoll presentation Autumn 2027. 
 Remote production phase late October 2026 to January 2027.\n\nMore: https:
 //www.ctm-festival.de/festival-2027/open-calls/in-listening-2027?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.ctm-festival.de/festival-2027/open-calls/in-listening-2027?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany. Premiered at CTM 2027 and broadcast on Deutschla
 ndfunk Kultur\, with onward presentation via ORF Oe1 (Zeit-Ton or Blaue St
 unde / Kunstradio) and/or ORF musikprotokoll im steirischen herbst in Graz
 . Applications accepted internationally\, submitted in English.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:camila-caneque-international-residency-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135731Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fundacion Camila Caneque: International Residency Program
 me 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Fundacion Camila Caneque\, with BAR project\, hosts a six-w
 eek international residency (8 October to 20 November 2026) titled In the 
 meantime nothing happens\, in the Emporda region of Catalonia. Open to art
 ists\, curators\, researchers\, and interdisciplinary practitioners\; the 
 residency covers a EUR 2\,000 gross stipend\, accommodation\, meals\, util
 ities\, round-trip travel\, insurance\, and curatorial support. Individual
 s only. Deadline 31 July 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Fundacion Camila Caneque w
 ith BAR project\nLocation: Emporda\, Catalonia\, Spain. Open international
 ly\; individuals only.\nAward: EUR 2\,000 gross stipend\, plus accommodati
 on\, meals\, utilities\, round-trip travel\, insurance\, and curatorial su
 pport. 6 weeks. No application fee.\nDuration: Residency 8 October to 20 N
 ovember 2026.\n\nMore: https://www.fundacioncamilacaneque.org/agenda/progr
 ama-internacional-de-residencia-2026/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.fundacioncamilacaneque.org/agenda/programa-internacional-de
 -residencia-2026/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referra
 l
LOCATION:Emporda\, Catalonia\, Spain. Open internationally\; individuals on
 ly.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:transmediale-pro-helvetia-digital-art-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135731Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260829
SUMMARY:Deadline: transmediale x Pro Helvetia Digital Art Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:The fifth iteration of transmediale's Digital Art Residency\, r
 un with the Swiss Arts Council Pro Helvetia\, awarded to one individual or
  collective working in digital art practices at the intersection of media 
 arts\, performance\, sound and moving image. THEME: the 2027 programme sit
 s under transmediale's 40th-anniversary framework RFC 40\, named after the
  early internet Request for Comments series\, and treats the festival as a
  counter-infrastructure: the call asks how a network stays legible to itse
 lf while surrounding structures break down\, and how technical paradigms c
 an be reconfigured into new cultural protocols outside extractive logics\,
  moving from critique to construction. Proposals should offer alternatives
  to how we understand\, respond to and shape the technological conditions 
 we inhabit. WHAT IS OFFERED: an artist fee of CHF 2\,000 per month for two
  months\; a CHF 15\,000 production grant supporting a new work or the cont
 inuation of an existing project\, open to all formats and building on the 
 research begun during the residency (the project must be completed by Dece
 mber 2027 at the latest)\; travel and accommodation for the festival and t
 he residency\; a shared modular working space at transmediale studio\; con
 nections to Berlin institutions and stakeholders\; a public presentation i
 n transmediale's year-round studio programme\; and the option of an online
  publication in transmediale's journal. STRUCTURE: kick-off with a present
 ation of the residency projects during transmediale 2027 (26 to 31 January
  2027\, attendance optional but strongly recommended)\; onboarding and the
  first hybrid stretch in May 2027\; the mandatory on-site month in Berlin 
 in June 2027\; and a second hybrid stretch including reporting in July 202
 7. Availability for the festival week and for the whole of June in Berlin 
 are treated as key prerequisites. TIMELINE: open call 16 July to 28 August
  2026 (23:59 CEST)\; selected residents announced October 2026. Applicatio
 ns are only accepted via transmediale's submission forms. Contact: info[at
 ]transmediale.de.\n\nOrganisation: transmediale (in cooperation with the S
 wiss Arts Council Pro Helvetia)\nLocation: Hybrid: remote plus on-site at 
 transmediale studio\, silent green Kulturquartier\, Berlin-Wedding\, Germa
 ny. RESTRICTED: applicants must hold Swiss nationality or permanent reside
 nce in Switzerland and be firmly established in the Swiss cultural scene (
 Pro Helvetia's general requirements apply).\nAward: Artist fee of CHF 2\,0
 00 per month across the two-month residency (CHF 4\,000)\, plus a producti
 on grant of CHF 15\,000 for the selected project\, plus travel and accommo
 dation for both the festival and the residency month. Duos and collectives
  may apply but the fee and the production grant stay the same and must be 
 shared. No application fee.\nDuration: Two-month hybrid residency between 
 mid-May and mid-July 2027\, with the whole of June 2027 on-site in Berlin 
 (mandatory)\n\nMore: https://transmediale.de/en/news/digital-art-residency
 -2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://transmediale.de/en/news/digital-art-residency-2027?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hybrid: remote plus on-site at transmediale studio\, silent green 
 Kulturquartier\, Berlin-Wedding\, Germany. RESTRICTED: applicants must hol
 d Swiss nationality or permanent residence in Switzerland and be firmly es
 tablished in the Swiss cultural scene (Pro Helvetia's general requirements
  apply).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-design-grant-scheme-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135731Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260819
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260820
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Design Grant Scheme 2026 (final round)
DESCRIPTION:The Stimuleringsfonds Design Grant Scheme (Deelregeling Vormgev
 ing) supports projects by designers\, design agencies\, observers and cult
 ural institutions working across product\, graphic\, spatial\, fashion\, t
 extile and social design. Solo projects receive EUR 10\,000-25\,000\; proj
 ects with partners up to EUR 50\,000\, with at least 20 percent co-financi
 ng. From 2026 the scheme runs two rounds per year rather than three\, and 
 this round opens 12 August 2026 at 15:00 CEST and closes 19 August 2026 at
  16:00 CEST. The procedure is two-phase and applications are ordered by lo
 ttery draw rather than by submission time\, so submitting early confers no
  advantage. Applicants must be registered with the Dutch Chamber of Commer
 ce (KvK).\n\nOrganisation: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Creative
  Industries Fund NL)\nLocation: Netherlands. Requires establishment in the
  Kingdom of the Netherlands and Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK) registrati
 on.\nAward: EUR 10\,000-25\,000 for a single executing party\; EUR 10\,000
 -50\,000 for projects with project partners. Minimum 20 percent co-financi
 ng required. Round budget EUR 650\,000 (2026 total EUR 1\,580\,000). No ap
 plication fee.\nDuration: Project-based.\n\nMore: https://www.stimulerings
 fonds.nl/en/grants/design-grant-scheme?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/design-grant-scheme?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands. Requires establishment in the Kingdom of the Netherla
 nds and Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK) registration.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-architecture-grant-scheme-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135731Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260819
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260820
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Architecture Grant Scheme 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Stimuleringsfonds Architecture Grant Scheme supports archit
 ects\, observers\, design agencies and cultural institutions on projects a
 cross the broad field of architecture\, including design research\, reflec
 tion and public debate as well as built work. Solo projects receive EUR 10
 \,000-25\,000\, projects with partners up to EUR 50\,000\, with at least 2
 0 percent co-financing. This round opens 13 August 2026 at 15:00 CEST and 
 closes 19 August 2026 at 16:00 CEST. From 2026 the scheme allocates places
  by notary-supervised lottery draw rather than by order of submission. App
 licants must be registered with the Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK).\n\nOr
 ganisation: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Creative Industries Fun
 d NL)\nLocation: Netherlands. Requires establishment in the Kingdom of the
  Netherlands and Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK) registration.\nAward: EUR
  10\,000-25\,000 for a single executing party\; EUR 10\,000-50\,000 with p
 roject partners. Minimum 20 percent co-financing. Round budget EUR 587\,94
 6 (2026 total EUR 1\,155\,000). No application fee.\nDuration: Project-bas
 ed.\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/architecture-grant
 -scheme?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/architecture-grant-scheme?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands. Requires establishment in the Kingdom of the Netherla
 nds and Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK) registration.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-design-sector-internationalisation-2026@artificialnou
 veau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135731Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260922
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260923
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Design Sector Internationalisation Gra
 nt Scheme 2026
DESCRIPTION:This scheme funds international activity by the Dutch design\, 
 architecture and digital culture sectors\, covering projects that take pla
 ce mainly abroad and require at least one international partner. Open to p
 rofessional makers\, observers\, design agencies and cultural institutions
 . Grants run EUR 10\,000 to EUR 50\,000 with at least 20 percent co-financ
 ing. The round runs 25 August 2026\, 15:00 CEST to 22 September 2026\, 16:
 00 CEST. From 2026 places are allocated by lottery draw rather than order 
 of submission. Activities in countries under a code-red travel advisory or
  subject to sanctions are excluded. Applicants must be registered with the
  Dutch Chamber of Commerce (KvK).\n\nOrganisation: Stimuleringsfonds Creat
 ieve Industrie (Creative Industries Fund NL)\nLocation: Netherlands-based 
 applicants\; funded activity takes place mainly abroad. At least one inter
 national partner required.\nAward: EUR 10\,000 to EUR 50\,000. Minimum 20 
 percent co-financing. Round budget EUR 300\,000 (2026 total EUR 600\,000).
  No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\; activities take place main
 ly abroad.\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/design-sect
 or-internationalisation-grant-scheme?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/design-sector-internationali
 sation-grant-scheme?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refer
 ral
LOCATION:Netherlands-based applicants\; funded activity takes place mainly 
 abroad. At least one international partner required.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:waag-trust-me-im-an-airtist-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T135731Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Trust me\, I'm an AI/rtist: Open Call for Creative Interv
 entions
DESCRIPTION:Waag Futurelab invites artists\, theatre makers\, choreographer
 s\, dancers\, game designers and other creative practitioners to engage di
 rectly with seven experimental generative AI Enablers being co-created wit
 h technologists and dance\, theatre and gaming professionals. The call is 
 an invitation into the development process: selected artists get access to
  the technologies\, datasets\, interfaces and assumptions that shape these
  systems while they are still being built. Rather than testing whether the
  systems work\, artists are asked to interrogate why they work the way the
 y do\, who they are designed for\, what forms of creativity they enable or
  constrain\, and what assumptions about culture\, intelligence\, authorshi
 p\, labour\, bodies\, audiences and society are embedded in them. Waag is 
 looking for individuals and collectives willing to move beyond adoption in
 to investigation\, and welcomes proposals that are speculative\, critical\
 , poetic\, provocative\, humorous\, performative\, constructive or disrupt
 ive\, including work that challenges\, misuses\, reimagines\, hacks\, subv
 erts or plays with the tools\, exposes hidden biases\, questions environme
 ntal costs\, or imagines alternative technological futures. THE SEVEN AI E
 NABLERS\, each requiring an on-site visit to its technology partner: the G
 eneric Procedural Content Generation Enabler (text-to-3D assets and avatar
 s\, CERTH\, Greece)\; the Data-Driven Cultural Content Adaptation Enabler 
 (audience-aware creative content ideation with ranked candidate ideas\, CE
 RTH\, Greece)\; the Cross-Domain Audience Engagement Analytics Enabler (tu
 rning heterogeneous cultural participation data into interpretable engagem
 ent signals\, The Audience Agency\, Warrington\, UK)\; the Dance Style Ana
 lysis and Generation Enabler (dance video into virtual 3D choreography\, d
 issected into body\, effort\, shape and space components\, Centre of Excel
 lence for Research & Innovation\, Cyprus)\; the Immersive Design Integrati
 on Enabler for Dance & Theatre (NLP-driven XR environments with speech-to-
 3D scene editing\, Cyprus)\; the Music-to-Movement Translation Enabler (au
 dio into a time-aligned feature set spanning genre classification\, emotio
 nal valence-arousal analysis\, rhythm extraction and latent-space projecti
 on\, feeding motion generation\, spatial audio and visual choreography\, A
 ristotle University of Thessaloniki\, Greece)\; and the Adaptive Narrative
  Enabler for Games & Theatre (an evolutionary AI trained on creator-writte
 n story elements that generates infinite story variations\, explicitly rej
 ecting LLMs because of their dependence on copyrighted or public-domain co
 rpora that encode 19th and early 20th century sexism\, racism and imperial
 ism\, CAUSA Creation\, Austria). ELIGIBILITY: artists\, designers\, creati
 ve technologists\, theatre makers\, dancers\, choreographers and game desi
 gners\, as individuals or collectives\; applicants must hold a European VA
 T number. An info session with live demonstrations of the AI Enablers runs
  31 July 2026\, 10:00 to 11:30 CEST (meeting ID 995 7016 2341). Applicatio
 ns go through Homerun using the official Application Template\, uploaded a
 s a PDF\; read the Guide for Applicants\, which contains the full Enabler 
 descriptions\, before applying. Questions: zoenie at waag dot org. The AI 
 Enablers and this call are part of the Horizon Europe project HAMLET\, whi
 ch aims to make generative AI accessible to cultural organisations of all 
 sizes. Closes 30 September 2026\, 23:59 CEST. Free to apply.\n\nOrganisati
 on: Waag Futurelab (Horizon Europe project HAMLET)\nLocation: Europe. Enga
 ging with a specific AI Enabler includes an on-site visit to its technolog
 y partner: CERTH (Greece)\, The Audience Agency (Warrington\, UK)\, the Ce
 ntre of Excellence for Research & Innovation (Cyprus)\, Aristotle Universi
 ty of Thessaloniki (Greece)\, or CAUSA Creation (Austria). Final presentat
 ions September 2027.\nAward: EUR 20\,000 commission fee excluding VAT\, in
 clusive of artist fee\, travel\, accommodation and production costs. Appli
 cants must have a VAT number in Europe. No application fee.\nDuration: Jan
 uary to September 2027\, with final presentations in September 2027\n\nMor
 e: https://waag.org/en/article/open-call-creative-interventions-trust-me-i
 m-airtist/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://waag.org/en/article/open-call-creative-interventions-trust-me-i
 m-airtist/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Europe. Engaging with a specific AI Enabler includes an on-site vi
 sit to its technology partner: CERTH (Greece)\, The Audience Agency (Warri
 ngton\, UK)\, the Centre of Excellence for Research & Innovation (Cyprus)\
 , Aristotle University of Thessaloniki (Greece)\, or CAUSA Creation (Austr
 ia). Final presentations September 2027.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
